Day 1 - Git Advanced

1.)Branch :- Movable Pointer Pointing to commit.
Commands :- a.)git branch b.)git branch <name>

2.)checkout :- Switch from one branch to another.
Commands :- a.)git checkout <bname> b.)git checkout -b <bname>

3.)Cherry-Pick :- Take changes from one specific commit to other branch as a new commit.
Commands :- a.)git cherry-pick <chash>

4.)Tag :- Fixed refrence/label pointing to a specific commit.
Command :- a.)git tag <name>

5.)Merge :- Combine the history/changes of one branch into another branch.
Command :- a.)git merge <bname>

6.)Rebase :- Moves your branch base to another commit and replays your branch commits on top of it.
Command :- a.)git rebase <bname>

7.)Conflict :- Conflicts occurs when git cannot automatically usderstand wat changes should be combined.

8.)Squash :- Combines multiple commits into one commit.

9.)Reword :- Changes commit's message.

10.)Edit :- tell rebase to stop at particular commit so you can modify it.
~N means go back N generation. ^N means select parent.

11.)Submodules :-Git repo included inside another git repo.
Command :- a.)git submodule add <RURL> b.)git submodule update --init --recursive c.)git clone --recurse-submodules <RURL> d.)git submodule update --remote

12.)Branching Strategy :- Teams rule for creating using naming and merging branches.

13.)Feature branch :- Always usefull, because it isolates your work from main. Allowing parellel development, testing, review, and safe merging.

NOTE :- As a team member, my responsiblity is to work on my branch, keep my branch updated with the latest main,write clean and tested code, commit meaningfull changes, push my branch, create a PR, participate in code review, resolve conflicts when required.

ONE LINER :-
Branch    → movable pointer to a commit
Checkout  → switch branch
Merge     → combine branches
Rebase    → replay commits on a new base
Conflict  → Git can't automatically combine changes
Cherry-pick → apply a specific commit's changes elsewhere
Tag       → fixed label/reference to a commit
Squash    → combine commits
Reword    → change commit message
Edit      → stop and modify a commit
~         → go backward N generations
^         → select a parent
Submodule → Git repo inside another Git repo
Feature branch → isolated development branch
